# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your notes are yours.
#
# This kit tracks its own scaffolding — docs, scripts, skills, templates and
# the Example spoke. It does NOT track what you write. That means you cannot
# accidentally push your second brain to a public remote, and `git status`
# stays readable instead of listing every note you touched today.
#
# Note on syntax: git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is
# excluded, so everything below ignores directory *contents* (`dir/*`) rather
# than the directory itself. Keep that shape if you edit this.
#
# Spokes you create are added here by scripts/new_spoke.sh, at the bottom.
# Want to track one deliberately — a public research notebook, say? Delete its
# line. See docs/VERSIONING.md before you do.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Your personal layer ---------------------------------------------------
_self/*
!_self/self-interview.md
!_self/README.md

# --- Raw and sensitive material -------------------------------------------
_private/*
!_private/.gitkeep
!_private/watchlist.example.txt

# --- Your inbox and generated briefs ---------------------------------------
_inbox/*
!_inbox/.gitkeep
!_inbox/briefs
_inbox/briefs/*
!_inbox/briefs/.gitkeep

# --- Weekly idea logs (the cross-domain map itself stays tracked) ----------
_maps/ideas/*
!_maps/ideas/.gitkeep

# --- Ingest staging and script backups ------------------------------------
**/_staged/
**/_processed/
*.bak

# --- OS, editor and language noise ----------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Obsidian window state (vault config itself is fine to keep) ----------
.obsidian/workspace*
.obsidian/cache

# --- Your spokes (added automatically by scripts/new_spoke.sh) ------------
